# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# .env.example — the live configuration with secrets removed.
#
# Generated from the running .env so it reflects what is ACTUALLY configured,
# not what was configured whenever someone last remembered to update this file.
# Every tuned value below is the real one and carries the reasoning that
# produced it.
#
# Secrets and personal details are blank. Fill them in and rename to .env.
#
# Regenerate after changing configuration:
#   .venv/bin/python make_env_example.py
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────


# ══ TUNED FOR EVIDENCE RATE — 2026-08-26 (revised) ══════════════════════════
# Settings below maximise TRADES per day subject to staying net positive, not
# expected profit. This is paper trading: a trade costs nothing and data is the
# scarce thing, so optimising backtest profit while producing 0.7 trades a day
# was the wrong objective.
#
#   crypto  RSI ceiling removed (was 57). It was derived on ONE_HOUR SMA 5/30
#           and is harmful at SIX_HOUR 10/40 — 26 trades/+4.09 with it,
#           59 trades/+9.19 without. Better on BOTH axes. Settings do not
#           transfer across timeframes; re-derive them when the timeframe moves.
#
#   stocks  RSI band 30/70 -> 35/65, volume filter 1.0 -> 0.0.
#           59 trades/+12.40 -> 129 trades/+5.20. Deliberately trades expected
#           profit for evidence rate. Net stays clearly positive, which is the
#           constraint that keeps the data meaningful.
#
# Expected: ~1.6 trades/day combined, against ~0.72 before.
#
# ══ CONFIGURATION FREEZE — 2026-08-26, amended 2026-08-30 ═══════════════════
# Do not change strategy, thresholds or stops before 2026-10-10.
#
# Six config changes were made on 2026-08-26 alone. Each one resets the
# forward-test clock, and this system's feedback loop is measured in days per
# trade — so nothing ever ran long enough to produce evidence. Change velocity
# exceeded evidence velocity. That, not any single parameter, is why months of
# work produced no verdict.
#
# ── 2026-08-30: crypto amended, then reverted the same day ─────────────────
# Crypto was moved to ONE_HOUR to raise its evidence rate, then moved back
# after measuring what hourly can actually earn: gross 1.17%/trade against a
# 1.206% fee. It cannot clear its own costs at that timeframe, so the extra
# data would only have confirmed a loss that arithmetic already guaranteed.
#
# Net effect on configuration: none. Crypto is parked on SIX_HOUR as before.
# The lesson is recorded because it nearly repeated the pattern this freeze
# exists to stop — changing a setting to make a number move, without first
# checking whether the new setting could produce the outcome being sought.
#
# CRYPTO IS PARKED. 53 forward trades, 19% win rate, net -$2.18, fails 3 of 5
# criteria. The bots keep running so the record accrues at no cost, but crypto
# is not tuned again on backtest evidence. See the granularity block below.
#
# STOCKS CARRY THE TEST. Config unchanged and it has out-of-sample support:
# +$3.65 over 127 trades across 12 tickers. Twelve bots went live 2026-08-26,
# so the arm is four days old, not failing. Leave it alone until ~2026-09-27.
#
# EXPECTED RATE — judge against this number, not against a feeling:
#   stocks  12 bots, mean reversion 35/65   ~24 entries/month  (~1 per day)
#   crypto   9 bots, SMA 10/40 SIX_HOUR     ~14 entries/month  (~1 every 2 days)
#
# Judge STOCKS on the pooled count, not per ticker: the strategy is what is
# being tested, and 12 tickers reach 20 pooled trades ~12x faster than any one
# of them reaches it alone. The dashboard shows this row above the per-symbol
# cards.
#
# A day with zero trades is normal. A WEEK with zero stock trades is a signal —
# check restart_bots.py --check first, then the signal logs for blocked_by.
#
# CHECKPOINTS:
#   2026-09-27  ~20 POOLED stock trades — first read on the sign
#   2026-10-25  ~40 POOLED stock trades — enough to decide
#   crypto      no checkpoint. It is parked, not pending.
#
# WHY STOCKS CARRY THE TEST:
#   Stocks are commission-free; mean reversion was positive out-of-sample on
#   BOTH timeframes at ALL FOUR thresholds tested. Stable.
#   Crypto pays 1.207% a round trip, and the best variant FLIPS with the
#   timeframe (SMA wins at six-hour, mean reversion at hourly). That is the
#   signature of noise, not edge. Crypto is frozen as a slow control, not
#   because it is promising.
#
# Adding SYMBOLS is allowed during the freeze — it raises the evidence rate
# without changing what is being tested. Changing SETTINGS is not.
# ════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
# Coinbase Developer Platform (CDP) API Credentials
# Create these keys at https://portal.cdp.coinbase.com/
COINBASE_API_KEY=
COINBASE_API_SECRET=

# Active Trading Profile
# Options: CONSERVATIVE, AGGRESSIVE, HYPER
ACTIVE_PROFILE=CONSERVATIVE

# Trading Settings
# Set DRY_RUN to True to simulate trades without executing them on Coinbase
DRY_RUN=True

# The product pair to trade (e.g., BTC-USD, ETH-USD)
TRADING_PAIR=BTC-USDC

# Amount of USD to use per trade (ensure this satisfies Coinbase's minimum requirements)
TRADE_AMOUNT_USD=10.0

# How often the bot runs its strategy loop (in seconds)
LOOP_INTERVAL_SECONDS=60

# The timeframe/candlestick size for the strategy (e.g. ONE_MINUTE, ONE_HOUR)
# ONE_HOUR gives meaningful price swings (1-3%) that can clear the 1.20% roundtrip fee
GRANULARITY=ONE_HOUR

# Broad-market regime filter (minimum percentage of bullish assets required to buy)


